// AppendRevisionWithBodyWithResponse Append a revision.
//
// **Always appends. Nothing is overwritten**, so there is no `If-Match`
// and no `412`: two people appending from the same base produce two
// revisions, both in history, the second current. The response says which
// revision this append produced and which one was current when the
// request was read — a gap between `followed.seq` and `revision.seq`
// means somebody else appended in between, which is E8's to render
// ("someone else appended while you were typing") rather than the
// server's to refuse.
